Retro Cluster icon (icon.png) uses the original DSEG7 Classic Bold atlas glyphs
and the application tachometer colours. Generated by tools/make-app-icon.py.
DSEG attribution and SIL OFL terms are retained below.

Centre widget extension: centre_widgets.js renders tyre readings, vehicle information, and unavailable music/navigation views with the retained DSEG and Roboto atlases. Music artwork/timeline support is a bounded internal display contract, not an established BMW or CarPlay reader. No BC interface, media transport or map service is added. Original atlas pixels and licenses are unchanged. See docs/WIDGETS.md.

Russian label atlases: Roboto Condensed SemiBold, Copyright 2011 The Roboto Project Authors (https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto-classic), SIL Open Font License 1.1. Full license: licenses/RobotoCondensed-OFL.txt. Original seven-segment atlases remain unchanged. The enlarged status-line atlas ru_status.json uses this same Roboto Condensed SemiBold face at 28px, cell height 31px and baseline 26; reproducible recipe: tools/bake_status_font.py.

Unused development resource d7_drive.json (not rendered by the current profile layouts): the original d7_big.json pixel data and numeric metrics are copied unchanged. Full-size D/S/M/P/R/N are a separately identified project extension assembled from the original DSEG segment masks, with added geometric strokes: S reuses the original 5; R/N use explicit diagonals, M uses two diagonals, and D includes a continuous left stem. These extensions are not represented as unmodified upstream glyphs. DSEG font copyright (c) 2017, keshikan (http://www.keshikan.net), with Reserved Font Name "DSEG", under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 reproduced below. This additional atlas does not replace or modify the original d7_big/d7_gear files. Its reproducible development recipe is tools/bake_drive_font.py; tools/bake_gear_program.py is a compatibility wrapper for that generator and no longer produces a separate small Roboto atlas. The original TTF and OFL are retained in tools/fonts-src/ in the development project.

Tachometer shader retro_tachometer.js is derived from SHIFTBAR in bimmer-lab/apps shared/shaders.js, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 bimmer-lab, pinned in UPSTREAM.lock.json. This derivative retains the Retro segment form and uses eighty equal 100rpm cells on the linear 0..8000rpm axis. Active profiles retain fixed green/yellow/red visual zones below 7000rpm. At valid readings of 7000rpm or above, all eighty cells flash red, alternating bright and dim (alpha 0.18) phases every 250ms using the existing update tick; the source reading and computed fill remain unchanged. Missing RPM cancels flashing, and archival original mode retains the upstream warning/flash behavior. shared/hud.js adds the protected _effectShader(w) extension hook; the application selects its derivative only for the active profile tachometer, while archival original mode selects the upstream shader. Original attribution and licenses are retained below.

Retro Cluster 0.2.0 derives from the pinned bimmer-lab/apps Retro 80s.
The adapted tachometer also contains a dormant six-pixel blue cap for a future verified active cold-engine RPM restriction. No such passive source was identified in the pinned repositories: the cap stays hidden in the current car and bench profiles. This is a project display extension, not a verified reproduction of BMW's factory indicator. It does not use a timer, oil-temperature estimate or learned maximum. Existing red flashing takes priority; the archival shader is unchanged. See docs/COLD_RPM_SIGNAL.md.
Drive-mode enums and additional read-only source semantics are adapted from cauliflowermossgrape/idrive7-apps (MIT), pinned in UPSTREAM.lock.json; exact source files and limitations are documented in docs/DATA_SOURCES.md. Original notices follow unchanged. This derivative includes the original DSEG7 and Barlow HUD atlases, the retained, unused d7_drive development atlas, and separate Roboto Condensed Cyrillic label atlases; other fonts mentioned below are retained as upstream attribution.
